### 0g. [2026-02-25 13:28] --immediately-restrict-first-session
introduce a --immediately-restrict-first-session (otherwise, the default is to allow running, no matter it is in the evening, or even after work-hour-start), when --immediately-restrict-first-session is given (not default) we should immediately pause (if it is during the pause time window)

### 0h. [2026-02-26 05:00] --verse-count
give me a new feature --step (or your suggestion), that we only work for --step n (n verses) and quit.

rename it with --verse-count instead of --limit (and do a number format check), default 10

no, change it. with no --verse-count, it is unlimited. and with --verse-count but no number, it is 10 by default, and with --verse-count n , it is n verses.

### 0i. [2026-02-26 08:54] --till with duration and clock time
give me a new feature --till/--untill followed by 30 min or 45 minute or 50 minutes or 1 hr or 3 hrs or 2 hour or 3 hours and then quit.

for --till, we also accept 17:50; 21:00;etc, but check that the time is in the future.

### 0j. [2026-02-26 09:21] Session report formatting
for the final report, don't need to print the skipped (previously done) part. Just print the works done at this session (before quit), also I need how long it takes per verse (m/v)

### 0k. [2026-02-26 09:34] Token-out detection
